Measured (oplog_20261008): MEmptyZ stop -> next move, 78 gaps, min 1015 ms / median 1594 ms = C_Empty_Up OnDelayTime 10, served again on every scan of `A.Pop() && B.Pop() && Select.Pop() && C_Empty_Up.Push()` because golden Push / Pop end with Task=1.

mycylin.cpp (same-line additions + an EOF block; no line moves, no class layout change): a completed Push / Pop marks the Cylinder[] slot confirmed on / off; OnSwitch / OffSwitch (On, Push / Off, Pop) clear the opposite mark; while marked and the cylinder HAS that sensor and it still reads in position, Push / Pop return true at once. No sensor, sensor dropped, raw On(), other machines = golden. Armed by g_W906CylNoReDelayHook, set in JsonBridge/W906DualCoil9050.cpp's registrar (HT9050 test as the paired coil hook).

tests/test_dualcoil9050.cpp [6]: first Push 313 ms, again at once; sensor lost -> not in position; back -> settles once (312 ms) then at once; Pop the same; raw On waits; no On sensor waits; not HT9050 waits (control). 35/35.
ctest (build_integ_dbg_x86, 24 cylinder / HT9050 tests): 21 pass; MotorPoints_HT9050 / MachineSuckers_HT9050 / MachineMotors_HT9050 fail on table values pinned before today's Mot_Table / IO_Table edits (home speeds, sucker addresses) -- no cylinder code involved.
